Pushing boulders in holes is hard?  Ummm... not for me.
I just count the boulders and count the holes.

   Easiness = (Boulders - Holes);

Take a pickaxe along and the first two levels are ridiculously
easy.  You can axe or corner up to Easiness boulders if they're
in the way.  Just make sure you don't axe or corner more than
Easiness boulders and the game's a breeze.

The top 2 levels get a bit more logically demanding, in that
Easiness is often only 2 or 3.  (So you can't axe or corner
more than a boulder or two without making the game unwinnable.)
But it's really just a matter of thinking how to shove rocks
around without cornering them.  That may require, on some levels,
pushing boulders several rooms AWAY FROM the holes in order to
get them in a position where you can get behind them and push
them back the other way.  But that's still child's play.

The more interesting situations are where it's required to
circle around through several rooms to push a boulder from a
different direction, then circle around and push it from yet
another direction.

(I might try a blessed scroll of earth in Sokoban sometime,
and see what that does.  If it makes more boulders, it would
make things even easier.)

For me, the only really HARD things about Sokoban are:

1. Easy to die of starvation.
2. Pets or monsters get behind boulders and make them
   unmovable.  Esp. bad in Hole Row.
3. Random monsters (sometimes really nasty ones like dragons)
   attack you when you least expect it.  Esp. bad if you've
   just dropped all your armor and weapons in order to squeeze
   between two boulders.

But it's all just part of the challenge, really.

